---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Galaxies Cheat Sheet | Free Spiral, Elliptical, Irregular, Dark Matter"
  description="Complete galaxies cheat sheet with spiral, elliptical, irregular galaxies and dark matter. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Galaxies<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Spiral, elliptical, irregular galaxies and dark matter. From local group to large-scale structure.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Galaxy Types</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Spiral Galaxies</h3>
        <pre><code>Flat disk with spiral arms
Young stars in arms
Old stars in bulge
Gas and dust in disk
Examples: Milky Way, Andromeda</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Elliptical Galaxies</h3>
        <pre><code>Spherical to elliptical shape
Old stars, little gas/dust
No spiral structure
Range of sizes: dwarf to giant
Examples: M87, Centaurus A</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Irregular Galaxies</h3>
        <pre><code>No regular shape
Often result of collisions
Rich in gas and dust
Active star formation
Examples: Large Magellanic Cloud</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Dark Matter</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Galaxy Rotation Curves</h3>
        <pre><code>v(r) = √(GM(r)/r)
If M(r) = const: v ∝ 1/√r (Keplerian)
Observation: v ≈ const at large r
Implies M(r) ∝ r (dark matter halo)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Large-Scale Structure</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Hierarchy</h3>
        <pre><code>Stars → Star clusters → Galaxies
Galaxies → Galaxy groups → Galaxy clusters
Clusters → Superclusters → Cosmic web
Void: regions with few galaxies</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Active Galactic Nuclei</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>AGN Types</h3>
        <pre><code>Quasar: extremely luminous AGN
Seyfert galaxy: moderate AGN
Blazar: jet pointed at Earth
Radio galaxy: strong radio emission
Powered by supermassive black hole accretion</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
